# Testing rules

- Run repository suites through Make targets and tee long output under `/tmp`.
- Never skip, gate, weaken, or delete a failing assertion to make tests pass.
- Every Agent behavior change or feature requires a released-Dex server
  integration test and a full-stack browser E2E test.
- Full-stack E2E uses the real HTTP API and asserts visible DOM state, focus,
  keyboard behavior, and user interactions. Do not use route fulfillment or
  stop at an HTTP success assertion.
- Fix production code when a test exposes a discrepancy. Never preserve a bug
  by changing the expected behavior.
- Async tests use unique Flow IDs and deadline polling, not sleeps.
- Test Worker replacement at durable waits and side-effect boundaries.
- Default tests are deterministic. Only the explicit live OpenAI target loads
  the ignored root `.env`, runs serially, and keeps credentials out of output.
